    "reasons": "The Lean statement does not faithfully capture the geometric problem. D is only required to lie on the circumcircle, not to be diametrically opposite A. The condition h₄ says E lies in segment AD, while h₅ says D is the midpoint of AE; these are incompatible for the nondegenerate triangle intended, since E should lie on the line AD beyond D, not in segment AD. The line l is declared as line[E,D], i.e. essentially line AD, rather than the line through E perpendicular to AE. Moreover, F and G are only constrained to lie on lines AB and AC respectively, not to lie on l, so FG is essentially unconstrained by the assumptions. The variable l also appears without being explicitly declared in the theorem binders, which is a structural issue. Overall, the formalization misses key geometric constraints and therefore does not express the intended theorem.",
